    "text": "In a right-angled triangle \\(\\triangle ABC\\) where \\(\\angle B = 90^\\circ\\), the side opposite to angle \\(\\theta\\) is 3 cm and the hypotenuse is 5 cm. What is \\(\\sin \\theta\\)?",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)",
        "isCorrect": true
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "\\(\\frac{4}{5}\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "\\(\\frac{5}{3}\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "solution": "**Step 1: Formula**\n\\(\\sin \\theta = \\frac{\\text{Opposite side}}{\\text{Hypotenuse}}\\).\n**Step 2: Substitution**\nOpposite side = 3, Hypotenuse = 5.\n\\(\\sin \\theta = \\frac{3}{5}\\).\n**Step 3: Conclusion**\n\\(\\sin \\theta = \\frac{3}{5}\\).",
