    "questionCode": "MH-9-MTH2-9-9.1.1-OSC-101",
    "text": "Find the slant height \\(l\\) of a right circular cone whose base radius is 3 cm and height is 4 cm.",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "5 cm (alt 1)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "4 cm",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "7 cm",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "5 cm",
        "isCorrect": true
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "D",
    "solution": "**Step 1: Formula**\nSlant height \\(l = \\sqrt{r^2 + h^2}\\).\n**Step 2: Calculation**\n\\(l = \\sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 16} = \\sqrt{25} = 5\\text{ cm}\\).\n**Step 3: Conclusion**\nThe slant height is 5 cm.",
